.TH GIT-@ 1 "August 2025" "GitAT v1.1.0" "Git Workflow Management Tool"
.SH NAME
git-@ \- Git Workflow Management Tool
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B git @
[\fICOMMAND\fR] [\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
GitAT (Git @) is a comprehensive Git workflow management tool that extends Git with workflow management capabilities. It provides commands for branch management, commit organization, pull request creation, and more, all following best practices and conventions.
.PP
GitAT uses Git's built-in extension mechanism, so once installed, \fBgit @\fR will be available as a native Git command.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B work <type> <description>
Create work branches following Conventional Commits
.TP
.B hotfix <description>
Create hotfix branches for urgent fixes
.TP
.B save "message"
Securely save changes with validation
.TP
.B squash [branch]
Squash commits with auto-detection of parent branch
.TP
.B pr [options]
Create Pull Requests with auto-description generation
.TP
.B sprout
Manage working branch configuration
.TP
.B sweep
Clean up local branches (merged + remote-deleted)
.TP
.B info
Comprehensive status report from all commands
.TP
.B shasum
Detailed branch status and commit relationships
.TP
.B logz
View commit history
.TP
.B product [<name>]
Product name configuration
.TP
.B feature [<name>]
Feature name configuration
.TP
.B issue [<id>]
Issue/task identifier configuration
.TP
.B semver
Semantic versioning management
.TP
.B dub
Enhanced tag creation with version integration
.TP
.B release
Create releases with proper tagging
.TP
.B master, root
Switch to trunk branches
.TP
.B wip
Work in progress management
.TP
.B changes
View uncommitted changes
.TP
.B _label
Generate commit labels
.TP
.B _id
Generate unique project identifiers
.TP
.B _path
Get repository path
.TP
.B _trunk
Manage trunk branch configuration
.TP
.B ignore
Add patterns to .gitignore
.TP
.B setup-local
Initialize local repository with branch structure
.TP
.B setup-remote
Initialize remote repository with basic structure
.TP
.B main, master, root
Switch to trunk branches (main/master)
.TP
.B _security
Security utilities and status
.TP
.B _go
Initialize GitAT for current repository
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B -h, --help
Show help message
.TP
.B -v, --version
Show version information
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
Create a feature branch:
.RS
.nf
git @ work feature add-user-authentication
.fi
.RE
.PP
Save changes:
.RS
.nf
git @ save "Add user authentication system"
.fi
.RE
.PP
Create a pull request:
.RS
.nf
git @ pr
.fi
.RE
.PP
Clean up merged branches:
.RS
.nf
git @ sweep
.fi
.RE
.SH CONVENTIONAL COMMITS
.PP
GitAT follows the Conventional Commits specification:
.RS
.IP \(bu 2
\fBfeat:\fR New features (MINOR version)
.IP \(bu 2
\fBfix:\fR Bug fixes (PATCH version)
.IP \(bu 2
\fBdocs:\fR Documentation changes
.IP \(bu 2
\fBstyle:\fR Code style changes
.IP \(bu 2
\fBrefactor:\fR Code refactoring
.IP \(bu 2
\fBtest:\fR Adding tests
.IP \(bu 2
\fBchore:\fR Maintenance tasks
.IP \(bu 2
\fBhotfix:\fR Urgent fixes
.RE
.SH FILES
.PP
GitAT uses Git configuration to store project settings:
.RS
.IP \(bu 2
\fBat.product\fR - Product name
.IP \(bu 2
\fBat.feature\fR - Current feature name
.IP \(bu 2
\fBat.task\fR - Current task/issue ID
.IP \(bu 2
\fBat.branch\fR - Working branch
.IP \(bu 2
\fBat.trunk\fR - Trunk branch (master/main)
.IP \(bu 2
\fBat.version\fR - Current version
.IP \(bu 2
\fBat.wip\fR - Work in progress branch
.RE
